<title>ROMANIA: ROMANIA MTH/MTH INFLATION LEAPS TO 3.4 PCT IN OCT.</title>
<headline>ROMANIA MTH/MTH INFLATION LEAPS TO 3.4 PCT IN OCT.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romanian monthly inflation</p>
<p>jumped to 3.4 percent in October from 2.4 percent in September,</p>
<p>the National Statistics Board said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Year-on-year inflation was 45.1 percent in October, down</p>
<p>from 45.3 percent in September, with the ten-month consumer</p>
<p>price rise at 35.5 percent, up from 30.1 percent over</p>
<p>January-September.</p>
<p>The 1996 government forecast for 12-month inflation is 38</p>
<p>percent, up from a target of 20 percent agreed with the IMF,</p>
<p>which was later adjusted at 30 percent.</p>
<p> ROMANIAN INFLATION	OCTOBER    SEPTEMBER   OCTOBER 95</p>
<p> monthly CPI rise	   3.4	   2.4	   3.5</p>
<p> yr/yr rise		  45.1	  45.3	  24.3</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
</text>
